## Summary of the methods

**`groupRollbackRequestsBasedOnFileGroup(List<HoodieRollbackRequest>)`** — a convenience overload that delegates to the generic version, passing identity for request creation and method references such as `HoodieRollbackRequest::getPartitionPath`, `getFileId`, `getLatestBaseInstant`, `getLogBlocksToBeDeleted`, and `getFilesToBeDeleted`.

**`groupSerializableRollbackRequestsBasedOnFileGroup(List<SerializableHoodieRollbackRequest>)`** — the same pattern but for the serializable variant, using `SerializableHoodieRollbackRequest::new` as the constructor function and the corresponding getters.

**The generic `groupRollbackRequestsBasedOnFileGroup<T>`** does the actual work. Per its docstring, it groups requests so each file group has `"at most two non-empty rollback requests"` — one for the base file, one for log files. It builds a map keyed by partition/file-ID pairs, then consolidates log blocks to be deleted into a single request per file group, while keeping base/file-delete requests separate. It includes a defensive guard that logs a warning when both files-to-delete and log-blocks-to-delete are unexpectedly present, since `"Only one of the following should be non-empty."`

If you need the exact code, it's available directly from the Apache Hudi source repository under its Apache License 2.0.

